Adds support for explicit asm("reg") register parameters in function
declarations for the m68k-amiga-elf (Bartman/Abyss) toolchain.

Enables vbcc-style AmigaOS register parameter syntax on the callee side:

  void DevOpen(struct Library *dev  asm("a6"),
               struct IORequest *io asm("a1"),
               ULONG unit           asm("d0"),
               ULONG flags          asm("d1"));

When a function is compiled with register-constrained parameters, each
argument arrives directly in the named register with no stack frame slot.

Note: this patch covers the callee (function being compiled) side.
Calls to register-parameter functions from C still use the existing
inline-asm macro stubs in the NDK headers, as before.

Apply AFTER gcc-barto.patch from inside the gcc-15.1.0 source directory:

  patch -p1 < gcc-barto.patch
  patch -p1 < gcc-regparm.patch

--- a/gcc/config/m68k/m68k.h	2026-03-29 07:45:50.000000000 +0000
+++ b/gcc/config/m68k/m68k.h	2026-03-29 09:36:44.444382911 +0000
@@ -487,16 +487,29 @@
    XXX This macro is m68k specific and used only for m68kemb.h.  */
 #define NEEDS_UNTYPED_CALL 0
 
-/* On the m68k, all arguments are usually pushed on the stack.  */
-#define FUNCTION_ARG_REGNO_P(N) 0
+/* Data registers d0-d7 (hard regs 0-7) and address registers a0-a6
+   (hard regs 8-14) may be used as explicit parameter registers via an
+   asm("reg") constraint on the parameter declaration.  The frame pointer
+   (a5, reg 13), stack pointer (sp/a7, reg 15), and the virtual arg
+   pointer (reg 24) are excluded.  */
+#define FUNCTION_ARG_REGNO_P(N)					\
+  (((N) >= D0_REG && (N) <= D0_REG + 7)			\
+   || ((N) >= A0_REG && (N) <= A6_REG			\
+       && (N) != FRAME_POINTER_REGNUM))
 
-/* On the m68k, this is a single integer, which is a number of bytes
-   of arguments scanned so far.  */
-#define CUMULATIVE_ARGS int
